# JPA Entity Layer Rules
# Applies to: Domain models, entity classes, JPA annotations, validation

---

## Package Location

```
src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/
```

---

## Entity Class Hierarchy

```
BaseEntity (id, isNew)
├── NamedEntity (name)
│   ├── Pet
│   ├── PetType
│   └── Specialty
├── Person (firstName, lastName)
│   ├── Owner
│   └── Vet
├── Visit
├── User
└── Role
```

**When creating a new entity, extend the appropriate base class.**

---

## Entity Template

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model;

import jakarta.persistence.*;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.*;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation.JsonIgnore;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.*;

@Entity
@Table(name = "table_name")  // Plural, lowercase
public class EntityName extends BaseEntity {  // or NamedEntity, Person

    @Column(name = "column_name")  // snake_case
    @NotEmpty  // Validation
    private String fieldName;  // camelCase

    @Column(name = "date_field", columnDefinition = "DATE")
    private LocalDate dateField;

    // ManyToOne relationship
    @ManyToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "parent_id")
    private ParentEntity parent;

    // OneToMany relationship
    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "thisEntity", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<ChildEntity> children;

    // Getters and setters
    public String getFieldName() {
        return this.fieldName;
    }

    public void setFieldName(String fieldName) {
        this.fieldName = fieldName;
    }
}
```

---

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|------------|---------|
| Class name | Singular, PascalCase | `Owner`, `PetType` |
| Table name | Plural, lowercase | `owners`, `pet_types` |
| Property name | camelCase | `firstName`, `birthDate` |
| Column name | snake_case | `first_name`, `birth_date` |

